# Deferred migrations — authored for this app but NOT applied to production.
#
# Production was provisioned selectively (SQL-editor pastes + ad-hoc SQL), so
# some files existed in the repo but the live DB never ran them. All the
# feature migrations have since been applied one-at-a-time (2026-08-12):
#   - 20260725 orders.paid_amount/balance_due (partial-deposit tracking)
#   - 20260730 payments table + record_partial_payment RPC
#   - 20260730 reconcile_balance_payment RPC
#   - 20260721 wallet_mints_7d aggregate (materialized, see below)
#   - 20260722 production_state table + realtime publication
#   - 20260716 sgcoin_payout_requests + submit/approve/complete/reject RPCs
# The two realtime publications were applied via the pooler (session mode).
#
# NOTE: 20260721_publish_wallet_mints_7d_for_realtime.sql was DELETED because
# Postgres cannot publish views ("cannot add relation ... to publication" on
# every PG version). It is replaced by 20260812_materialize_wallet_mints_7d_
# for_realtime.sql, which turns the aggregate into a trigger-maintained
# singleton table (same read shape: select mint_count) and publishes the table.
#
# 20260711_referendum_referral_2027.sql is additionally INCOMPATIBLE with the
# production posts table (id is UUID; the migration inserts a text slug) and
# the referendum is retired anyway — keep it listed.
#
# The runner (scripts/applyMigrations.ts) skips every file listed here and
# reports it as "deferred" — remove a line to let that migration apply on the
# next run, or mark it applied-without-executing via:
#   npx tsx scripts/applyMigrations.ts --baseline <YYYYMMDD_filename.sql>

20260711_referendum_referral_2027.sql
